  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Which of the following equations is the rotational equivalent of Newton’s second law of motion for an object of constant mass?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\textup{force = mass} \\times \\textup{angular acceleration}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\textup{force = moment of inertia} \\times \\textup{angular acceleration}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\textup{torque = mass} \\times \\textup{angular acceleration}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\textup{torque = moment of inertia} \\times \\textup{angular acceleration}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
